# Project: Hero Kids Game System for Foundry VTT

## Stack & Environment
- **Target Platform:** Foundry VTT v12 / v13+ (ES Modules `.mjs`, Handlebars `.hbs`, plain CSS).
- **System ID:** `herokids` (all template paths must start with `systems/herokids/`).
- **No Build Step:** Write clean, modern vanilla ES2022+ JavaScript and standard CSS directly—no TypeScript, Webpack, Vite, or Tailwind compilation required.

## Foundry VTT Coding Conventions
- Use modern Foundry APIs (`foundry.utils.mergeObject`, `foundry.utils.deepClone`, `Roll`, `ChatMessage`).
- Always declare `static get defaultOptions()` or ApplicationV2 patterns cleanly, and guard event listeners with `if (!this.isEditable) return;`.
- Keep document data schema changes synchronized between `template.json` and the Actor/Item sheets.
- Never replace `system.health.value` and `system.health.max` with separate booleans; keep `value` and `max` numeric so Foundry token resource bars stay synchronized, and derive UI condition states from `max - value`.

## Hero Kids Game Rules (Strictly Enforce)
- **Dice Mechanics:** All checks use d6 dice pools where **only the single highest die counts** (`Nd6kh`).
  - If a pool is `0` (or reduced to `0` by penalties), roll **2d6 and keep the lowest** (`2d6kl`).
  - Never sum dice together; always compare the single highest die (ties go to the defender/target).
- **Combat & Damage:**
  - Every successful attack deals **1 damage** (plus any bonus damage from specific Powers/Equipment).
  - Opposed rolls compare Attacker's highest d6 vs. Defender's Armor highest d6. If Attacker > Defender, apply 1 damage.
- **Health Boxes:**
  - Standard Heroes have 3 boxes (`max: 3`): **Bruised**, **Hurt**, **KO**.
  - 4-box characters (`max: 4`) use: **Bruised**, **Hurt**, **Tired**, **KO**.
  - Boss monsters with 5+ boxes prepend extra **Bruised** boxes before **Hurt**, **Tired**, **KO**.
  - Being Bruised, Hurt, or Tired does **not** apply dice penalties in Hero Kids; only reaching **KO** knocks the character out of combat.
- **Action Economy & Items:**
  - Each turn allows 1 Move (up to 4 squares) and 1 Action (Attack, Use Power, Drink Healing Potion, etc.).
  - Drinking a **Healing Potion** restores 1 health box (heals 1 damage) and decrements `system.potions.value` by 1.
  - **Skills** (Tracking, Stealth, Athletics, Perception) grant **+1 bonus d6** to relevant ability checks when trained/checked.

## Editing & Output Rules
- Read existing files in `module/`, `templates/`, and `styles/` before making changes to match existing class names and CSS selectors.
- Make minimal, surgical diffs—do not rewrite unrelated files or rename existing CSS classes unless requested.

## Foundry VTT v14 Architecture Rules
- Target Foundry VTT v14 ONLY. Never use legacy V1 `ActorSheet`, `defaultOptions()`, `getData()`, `mergeObject()`, or jQuery `activateListeners(html)`.
- Always extend `HandlebarsApplicationMixin(foundry.applications.sheets.ActorSheetV2)`.
- Configure templates via `static PARTS = { sheet: { template: "systems/herokids/templates/actor/hero-sheet.hbs" } }`.
- Configure window size and form auto-save via `static DEFAULT_OPTIONS = { classes: ["herokids", "sheet", "actor"], position: { width: 760, height: 540 }, form: { submitOnChange: true }, actions: { ... } }`.
- Prepare template data in `async _prepareContext(options)` using `this.document` and `this.document.system`.
- Handle clicks using `data-action="actionName"` attributes in Handlebars and static methods in `DEFAULT_OPTIONS.actions`.
- In `.hbs` templates, wrap content in a standard `<div class="herokids-card">` (ApplicationV2 automatically provides the `<form>` wrapper when `tag: "form"` or `ActorSheetV2` is used—do not nest a second `<form>` tag inside the template).